// element CT. A List[compound] element is pointer-boxed and iterated via the
// CT_INT pointer iterator, so the scalar Int-keyed registries above cannot name a
// distinct adapter for it. These hold the compound adapters; the scalar Int path
// stays byte-identical. Each adapter names the typedef `blink_<Kind>Iterator_<tag>`
// and derefs the boxed carrier by value before handing it to the closure.
